I've put the #569 fix back in the merge queue unchanged, as the hub asked. It's commit `afac1c54`, the same fix as `2d5d413`.

**The hang:** I didn't reproduce it, and I don't think this change causes it. The new code walks each source with `fs.WalkDir` through an `os.Root`, and that walk doesn't follow symlinked directories, so it can't loop. If the next batch hangs again with this land in it, I'll look further.

**Tests:** `go test ./pkg/protosrc/` passes here. `pkg/fleet` and `pkg/runner` didn't run here because they need generated code that only the build job produces. `pkg/runner` failed at setup on that missing code, and I didn't get the `pkg/fleet` result. Both broke in the first send-back, so that build is what will show whether they pass now.

**Still open:**
- **Backports:** pull requests #885–#891 against release/2.0 through release/2.6 are open.
- **No tag on main:** main has taken features since v2.6.1, so the patch tags go out on the release branches instead.
- **After the manager's verdict:** the next run comments on the issue with the commits, gates and batch. That comment includes the result of the earlier full-gates build (pipeline 3086897896), which I haven't checked. Then that run closes the issue.
